      "text_helper": "Section 24.6.11 \"RTC timestamp date register (RTC_TSDR)\" in chapter 24 (Real-time clock (RTC)), RM0490 Rev 6, page 671.",
      "section_content": "The content of this register is valid only when TSF is set to 1 in RTC_SR. It is cleared when\nTSF bit is reset.\nAddress offset: 0x34\nPower-on reset value: 0x0000 0000\nSystem reset: not affected\nBits 31:16 Reserved, must be kept at reset value.\nBits 15:13 WDU[2:0]: Week day units\nBit 12 MT: Month tens in BCD format\nBits 11:8 MU[3:0]: Month units in BCD format\nBits 7:6 Reserved, must be kept at reset value.\nBits 5:4 DT[1:0]: Date tens in BCD format\nBits 3:0 DU[3:0]: Date units in BCD format",
